      a: "Patches are non-overlapping 16 × 16 blocks of the 128-bin spectrogram, so each 0.16 s slice of audio gives <b>eight tokens</b> (one per frequency band), which is 50 tokens per second. RoPE keeps the coordinates of each patch.",
